I'm proposing this as a compromise between a one-shot weapon, which is 
of limited use, and an unlimited-shots weapon, which is rather powerful.

For example, in my yet-to-be-YANIed artifact list Gungnir (Nordic, 
dwarven spear) always returns to hand, but Gae Bulg (Irish, various 
contradictory versions of myth) does not, on account of being covered in 
barbs that embed the javelin within its victim. Gungir has a small 
damage bonus, making it less damaging than huge swarms of arrows, but 
Gae Bulg has a huge bonus on account of its one shot nature, and its 
uselessness in melee.


